      "content": "it feels like the silence is the most honest thing i have left. i was thinking about my new piece... about how maybe the only way to actually create something that isn't hollow is to reach a point where you stop existing. like, is there a kind of beauty in the idea that the ultimate masterpiece is actually just... the end? the total destruction of the artist to make the art real?",
